# Line endings are pinned to LF because this repo's contents are SYNCED from
# urbankitstudio/urbankitstudio (`packages/cli`), not edited here.
#
# Without this the sync is at the mercy of whoever runs it. The first seed of
# the sibling atlas mirror was measured: 74 files differed between the monorepo
# and that repo's checkout, and only 9 of those were real content changes. The
# other 65 were a CRLF checkout on one side meeting LF sources on the other.
# Git's `core.autocrlf` happened to absorb them that time, but that is a
# per-machine setting -- a Linux runner or a contributor without it produces
# commits that change nothing, burying the ones that matter.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes the working tree LF everywhere, so what the sync
# copies in is byte-identical to what git already has and the diff is the real
# change and nothing else.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.json text eol=lf
